#: temp.glade:28442
msgid "Global Options"
msgstr "Ol Opsen bilong Olgeta"

#: temp.glade:28486 temp.glade:28514
msgid "The anchor specifies what page in a book a picture will appear on. It appears on the same page as its anchor in the text. You can alter the Anchor Ref by a few verses to change the page on which it appears.\n"
"\n"
"An Anchor Ref must consist of a book code, perhaps followed by L or R (in the case of a diglot), then a space, then an in-book location which contains a dot (period). In a scripture book, the in-book location is Chap.Verse where the Verse matches the \\v value precisely. In other books, the in-book location can be anything as long as it is unique in that book and contains a dot (period).\n"
"\n"
"Anchor Refs for Diglots use the L or R suffix on the 3-letter book code to indicate whether the picture is to be associated with the Primary (L) text or the Secondary (R) text.\n"
"\n"
"In the glossary book (GLO) there is special support for \\k Keywords\\k* where in-book location of k.keyword(s) will anchor a picture to the corresponding term. The in-book location must match the value of the \\k Keyword or phrase\\k* with its spaces removed. For example,\n"
"\n"
"    GLO k.Altar - would link it to \\k Altar\\k*\n"
"    GLO k.JohntheBaptist - would link a picture to\n"
"               a glossary entry \\k John the Baptist\\k*\n"
"\n"
"You can copy-and-paste a glossary word or phrase after typing GLO k. and PTXprint will automatically strip the spaces for you.\n"
"\n"
"Where there are no intervening anchors, you can anchor to the Nth paragraph of e.g. poetry or a keyterm definition, by specifying the paragraph number after an = sign. For example, GLO k.Harp=2 or PSA 23.4=3. This can avoid the need to insert an explicit milestone to anchor a cutout if there is a page or column break after the start of the verse."
msgstr "Anka i makim wanem pas long buk bai piksa i kamap long en. Piksa i kamap long sem pas wantaim anka bilong en long tekst. Yu ken senisim Anka Ref liklik ves long senisim pas we piksa i kamap long en.\n"
"\n"
"Anka Ref i mas gat kod bilong buk, na maski L o R i kam bihain (long diglot), na wanpela spes, na wanpela ples insait long buk i gat wanpela dot (poin). Long wanpela buk bilong Skripsa, ples insait long buk em Kapitel.Ves we Ves i mas sem stret wantaim \\v namba. Long ol narapela buk, ples insait long buk inap i stap wanem samting tasol sapos em i narapela long buk na i gat wanpela dot (poin).\n"
"\n"
"Anka Ref bilong ol Diglot i yusim L o R long las bilong 3-leta kod bilong buk long makim sapos piksa i bilong Pastaim tekst (L) o Namba Tu tekst (R).\n"
"\n"
"Long buk bilong glosari (GLO) i gat spesel sapot long \\k Keywords\\k* we ples insait long buk bilong k.keyword(s) i pasim wanpela piksa long dispela tok. Ples insait long buk i mas sem wantaim \\k Keyword o ol tok\\k* tasol ol spes i no stap. Olsem:\n"
"\n"
"    GLO k.Altar - i bai pasim wantaim \\k Altar\\k*\n"
"    GLO k.JohntheBaptist - i bai pasim wanpela piksa long\n"
"               wanpela glosari tok \\k John the Baptist\\k*\n"
"\n"
"Yu ken kopiim na pestim wanpela glosari tok o ol tok bihain long taipim GLO k. na PTXprint bai rausim ol spes yet.\n"
"\n"
"Sapos i no gat narapela anka namel, yu ken pasim long namba N paragraf bilong poetri o dispela bilong wanpela keyterm, long putim namba bilong paragraf bihain long wanpela = saen. Olsem, GLO k.Harp=2 o PSA 23.4=3. Dispela inap rausim nid bilong putim wanpela milestone long pasim wanpela cutout sapos i gat pas o kolum brek bihain long stat bilong ves."

