#: temp.glade:28707
msgid "The frame size determines how large the picture\n"
"will appear on the page.\n"
"\n"
"Span Width only allows a Top or Bottom vertical placement.\n"
"Column Width allows several other more precise placement \n"
"options: Before Verse, After Paragraph, or Cutout; and these\n"
"can have Left/Inner or Right/Outer Horizontal positioning set. \n"
" \n"
"When using single column layout, there is no\n"
"difference between Column Width and Span Width."
msgstr "Frem saiz i makim hamas bikpela piksa bai kamap long pas.\n"
"\n"
"Span Width i larim Antap o Daunbilo tasol.\n"
"Column Width i larim sampela narapela ples i stret moa: Bifor Ves, Bihain long Paragraf, o Cutout; na ol dispela\n"
"inap gat Left/Inner o Right/Outer Horizontal ples.\n"
" \n"
"Sapos yu yusim wanpela kolum tasol, i no gat\n"
"senis namel long Column Width na Span Width."

#: temp.glade:28730 temp.glade:28782
msgid "Several options here are extensions to the normal USFM\n"
"markup standard for illustrations and are not expected\n"
"to work in other software. But PTXprint allows a greater\n"
"level of control in placing pictures.\n"
"\n"
"Top: Above everything except the header line\n"
"Bottom: Below all verse text (and footnotes in diglot)\n"
"Before Verse: 'Here' where defined or before its Anchor Ref\n"
"After Paragraph: After this paragraph\n"
"Cutout: A notch/corner cut out of the text, starting at current line\n"
"\n"
"The above options may have other positioning parameters such\n"
"as: Left, Right, Center, no. of lines (up or down)."
msgstr "Sampela opsen hia i ekstensen long stret USFM\n"
"makap bilong ol piksa na i no gat tingting olsem ol bai\n"
"wok long narapela software. Tasol PTXprint i larim moa\n"
"kontrol long putim ol piksa.\n"
"\n"
"Top: Antap long olgeta samting long hap hedalain\n"
"Bottom: Daunbilo long olgeta ves tekst (na futnot long diglot)\n"
"Before Ves: 'Hia' we i makim o bifor long Anka Ref bilong en\n"
"After Paragraf: Bihain long dispela paragraf\n"
"Cutout: Wanpela hap o kona i kat aut long tekst, i stat long lain nau\n"
"\n"
"Ol opsen antap inap gat narapela ples seting olsem:\n"
"Left, Right, Center, namba bilong ol lain (antap o daun)."

#: temp.glade:28758
msgid "An image (illustration) can be scaled to the\n"
"given size. This is particularly useful for\n"
"cutout images, and can prevent them from\n"
"taking up too much space within the text."
msgstr "Wanpela piksa inap kamap bikpela o liklik long\n"
"saiz yu givim. Dispela i gutpela tumas long\n"
"ol cutout piksa, na i ken stopim ol long\n"
"kisim planti ples insait long tekst."

#: temp.glade:28824
msgid "The frame size determines the boundaries of where the\n"
"picture will appear on the page.\n"
"\n"
"Span Width only allows a Top or Bottom vertical placement.\n"
"\n"
"Column Width allows several other more precise placement \n"
"options: Before Verse, After Paragraph, or Cutout; and these\n"
"can have Left/Inner or Right/Outer Horizontal positioning set. \n"
" \n"
"Page (in Margins) is intended for pictures that will cover an\n"
"entire page (i.e. preventing any scripture text from being on\n"
"that page), but will still show the header.\n"
"\n"
"Page (to Edge) is intended for pictures (or more commonly\n"
"for maps) to fill the entire page, with no margins at all. \n"
"Captions should not be used with 'Page (to Edge)' images."
msgstr "Frem saiz i makim ol bortpela bilong ples\n"
"piksa bai kamap long pas.\n"
"\n"
"Span Width i larim Antap o Daunbilo tasol.\n"
"\n"
"Column Width i larim sampela narapela ples i stret moa: Bifor Ves, Bihain long Paragraf, o Cutout; na ol dispela\n"
"inap gat Left/Inner o Right/Outer Horizontal ples.\n"
" \n"
"Page (in Margins) em bilong ol piksa i karamapim\n"
"olgeta pas (olsem i no gat Skripsa tekst long\n"
"dispela pas), tasol hedalain i stap yet.\n"
"\n"
"Page (to Edge) em bilong ol piksa (o moa long ol map)\n"
"long pulap olgeta pas, i no gat margin at all.\n"
"Ol kepsen i no ken yusim wantaim ol 'Page (to Edge)' piksa."

#: temp.glade:28917
msgid "It is good typesetting practice to make people\n"
"look outwards from the gutter, so you can set\n"
"whether the image is to be mirrored just on \n"
"odd pages or even pages.\n"
"\n"
"Some artists' pictures do not take into account\n"
"the \"dirty left-hand\" culture. For example, it would\n"
"be \"awkward\" to use a picture where Jesus is healing\n"
"a person using his LEFT hand! What an insult!\n"
"\n"
"So this option allows the image to be mirrored (on\n"
"both pages) in order to make the left become right.\n"
"But you should check carefully to see what other\n"
"unwanted side effects this mirroring may cause.\n"
"\n"
"Note: This option will be grayed out if the picture has  \n"
"the \"Never Mirror\" setting checked on the Checklist tab."
msgstr "Em i gutpela pasin bilong typesetting long mekim ol man\n"
"lukluk i go aut long gutter, olsem na yu ken makim\n"
"sapos piksa i mas mirror long odd pas tasol o even pas.\n"
"\n"
"Sampela piksa bilong ol artist i no tingim\n"
"kalsa bilong \"doti left-han\". Olsem, bai i\n"
"\"hevi\" long yusim piksa we Jisas i oraitim\n"
"wanpela man long LEFT han bilong em! Dispela i bikpela bagarap!\n"
"\n"
"Olsem na dispela opsen i larim piksa i mirror (long\n"
"olgeta tupela pas) long mekim left i kamap right.\n"
"Tasol yu mas lukim gut ol narapela hevi i no gutpela\n"
"mirror i ken kamapim.\n"
"\n"
"Toktok: Dispela opsen bai i kamap gre sapos piksa i gat\n"
"\"Never Mirror\" seting i makim long Checklist tab."

#: temp.glade:28935
msgid "Mirror:"
msgstr "Mirror:"

#: temp.glade:28950
msgid "Never = The image will never be mirrored\n"
"Odd = Mirrored only if image ends up on an odd page\n"
"Even = Mirrored only if image ends up on an even page\n"
"Always = Always mirrored (regardless of where it ends up)\n"
"\n"
"Note that if this option is grayed out, it is because \n"
"you have already restricted the mirroring options \n"
"on the Checklist tab."
msgstr "Never = Piksa i no inap mirror\n"
"Odd = Mirror sapos piksa i go long odd pas tasol\n"
"Even = Mirror sapos piksa i go long even pas tasol\n"
"Always = Mirror oltaim (maski em i go we)\n"
"\n"
"Tingim olsem sapos dispela opsen i gre, em i bikos\n"
"yu bin pasim pinis ol mirror opsen\n"
"long Checklist tab."

#: temp.glade:28985 temp.glade:29012
msgid "Some vertical position options allow a picture\n"
"to be moved up or down by a number of lines\n"
"or paragraphs.\n"
"\n"
"-Negative (minus) values specify to move UP.\n"
"+Positive (plus) values specify to move DOWN.\n"
"\n"
"Negative counts for cutouts raise the image,\n"
"but the cutout will not affect earlier paragraphs. \n"
"Note that negative and fractional paragraph \n"
"counts are invalid."
msgstr "Sampela vertikal ples opsen i larim wanpela piksa\n"
"long muv i go antap o daun long sampela lain\n"
"o paragraf.\n"
"\n"
"-Negatif (minus) namba i makim long muv i go ANTAP.\n"
"+Positif (plus) namba i makim long muv i go DAUN.\n"
"\n"
"Negatif namba bilong ol cutout i litimapim piksa,\n"
"tasol cutout i no ken senisim ol paragraf i go pastaim.\n"
"Tingim olsem negatif na hap namba bilong paragraf\n"
"i no stret."

#: temp.glade:29064
msgid "Can be used in Print/PDF publications. "
msgstr "Inap yusim long ol Print/PDF buk. "

#: temp.glade:29080
msgid "Can be used in mobile phone Apps. "
msgstr "Inap yusim long ol App bilong mobail fon. "

#: temp.glade:29096
msgid "Can be used on websites. "
msgstr "Inap yusim long ol websait. "

#: temp.glade:29117
msgid "If the image is from the recognized\n"
"set of pictures commonly used in\n"
"Scripture publications, then there is\n"
"no need to fill in the Copyright \n"
"Attribution field, as this will be\n"
"generated automatically for you."
msgstr "Sapos dispela piksa i stap insait long ol piksa\n"
"ol i save yusim long ol buk bilong Skripsa,\n"
"na i no gat nid long pulim Copyright\n"
"Attribution field, long wanem dispela bai\n"
"i kamap yet long em yet."

#: temp.glade:29125
msgid "Automatic"
msgstr "Otomatik"

#: temp.glade:29137
msgid "© ..."
msgstr ""

#: temp.glade:29142
msgid "Credit Overlays...\n"
"Some artists (e.g. David C Cook) require that\n"
"each image has a copyright message printed\n"
"on the image itself. The text and location can\n"
"be set here."
msgstr "Credit Overlays...\n"
"Sampela artist (olsem David C Cook) i laik olgeta piksa\n"
"i gat wanpela toktok bilong copyright i stap\n"
"long piksa yet. Ken makim tekst na ples bilong en\n"
"long hia."

#: temp.glade:29164
msgid "Credit overlay position and style"
msgstr "Ples na stail bilong credit overlay"

#: temp.glade:29210
msgid "Click to edit the Figure Caption properties on the Styles tab."
msgstr "Klikim long senisim ol propeti bilong Figure Caption long Styles tab."

#: temp.glade:29246
msgid "Extra:"
msgstr "Extra:"

#: temp.glade:29355
msgid "Use this tab to change the position, location, size \n"
"or orientation of the images.\n"
"\n"
"Note: Any changes you make here will NOT be \n"
"reflected in the Paratext USFM files. So if you are \n"
"changing an illustration, its caption or frame size\n"
"(column or span), then it is advisable to do so\n"
"in Paratext before regenerating the PicList here."
msgstr "Yusim dispela tab long senisim ples, saiz o pasin bilong\n"
"ol piksa i sanap.\n"
"\n"
"Not: Ol senis yu mekim long hia i NO inap kamap\n"
"long ol Paratext USFM fail. Olsem na sapos yu laik\n"
"senisim wanpela piksa, caption bilong en o saiz bilong frame\n"
"(column o span), orait gutpela yu mekim long\n"
"Paratext pastaim bipo yu kamapim gen PicList long hia."

#: temp.glade:29363
msgid "Details"
msgstr "Detels"

#: temp.glade:29420
msgid "Is there anything confusing or misleading in this image that the reader might misunderstand if they look at this picture apart from the text? Yes and no are both appropriate answers as some images may need to be seen alongside text in order to be understood."
msgstr "Ating gat wanpela samting long dispela piksa i mekim ol man i les o i no stret, na ol rider i ken kisim tingting i no stret sapos ol i lukim piksa tasol, i no gat tekst? Yes na No tupela i ken stret, long wanem sampela piksa i mas lukim wantaim tekst bambai ol i ken save."

#: temp.glade:29422
msgid "Is it clear what is happening in this image?"
msgstr "I klia long wanem samting i go het long dispela piksa?"

#: temp.glade:29433
msgid "First consider whether this picture is appropriate and culturally acceptable in any publications for this project."
msgstr "Pastaim tingim sapos dispela piksa i stret na kalsa i orait long olgeta pablikesen bilong dispela projek."

#: temp.glade:29435
msgid "Across Various Publications:"
msgstr "Long Ol Narapela Pablikesen:"

#: temp.glade:29449 temp.glade:29717 temp.glade:29771
msgid "Yes"
msgstr "Yes"

#: temp.glade:29467 temp.glade:29735 temp.glade:29789
msgid "No"
msgstr "No"

#: temp.glade:29505
msgid "Be sure that there is nothing offensive or inappropriate in this image. This could be the way people are clothed, what actions they are doing, how they are depicted, etc. “Culturally Appropriate” means this image is in a style from this culture or a related one, “Acceptable” means this picture might be from a different culture or in a different style, but there are no issues using it. “Inappropriate” means there are issues that should prevent this image from being used. Answering “Inappropriate” will help avoid this image being used in other publications."
msgstr "Lukim gut olsem i no gat wanpela samting long dispela piksa i mekim ol man i belhat o i no stret. Em inap long pasin bilong ol i werim klos, wanem pasin ol i mekim, o olsem wanem ol i soim ol, na ol narapela. “Culturally Appropriate” i min piksa i gat stail bilong dispela kalsa o narapela i klostu long en. “Acceptable” i min piksa inap kam long narapela kalsa o gat narapela stail, tasol i no gat hevi long yusim. “Inappropriate” i min i gat hevi i mekim olsem ol i no ken yusim dispela piksa. Sapos yu bekim “Inappropriate”, bai i helpim long no ken yusim dispela piksa long ol narapela pablikesen."

#: temp.glade:29507
msgid "Is this image acceptable in your culture?"
msgstr "Dispela piksa i orait long kalsa bilong yu?"

#: temp.glade:29518
msgid "Sometimes mirroring (reversing) an image makes it\n"
"acceptable since a left hand becomes a right hand, etc.\n"
"\n"
"Some artists' pictures do not take into account\n"
"the \"dirty left-hand\" culture. For example, it would\n"
"be \"awkward\" to use a picture where Jesus is healing\n"
"a person using his left hand!"
msgstr "Sampela taim sapos yumi tanim (tainim) piksa, em i kamap orait,\n"
"bikos han kais i kamap han sut, na olsem.\n"
"\n"
"Sampela piksa bilong ol artist i no tingim\n"
"pasin bilong \"han kais i doti\". Olsem, bai i no gutpela\n"
"sapos yumi yusim piksa we Jisas i helim wanpela man\n"
"wantaim han kais bilong em!"

#: temp.glade:29526
msgid "Would the image be culturally acceptable if \n"
"the image was mirrored (left becomes right)?"
msgstr "Sapos yumi tanim piksa (han kais i kamap han sut),\n"
"em i orait long kalsa o nogat?"

#: temp.glade:29538 temp.glade:29860
msgid "Now consider whether there are any issues with using this picture in this particular publication (config-specific)."
msgstr "Nau tingim sapos i gat wanpela hevi long yusim dispela piksa long dispela pablikesen (config-specific)."

#: temp.glade:29540
msgid "In This Publication:"
msgstr "Long Dispela Pablikesen:"

#: temp.glade:29556
msgid "Consider how this image is used alongside the text and what function it serves. Maybe it depicts a building or item from a biblical culture, or a scene from a story."
msgstr "Tingim olsem wanem dispela piksa i stap wantaim tekst na wanem wok em i mekim. Ating em i soim wanpela haus o samting bilong kalsa bilong Baibel, o wanpela senis bilong stori."

#: temp.glade:29558
msgid "Is this picture intended for: clarification,\n"
"story enhancement, filler, unknown?"
msgstr "Dispela piksa em bilong wanem: skelim klia,\n"
"mekim stori i strong, pulapim ples, o i no save?"

#: temp.glade:29570
msgid "Does the image support what the text is saying? As they read the passage does the image help in their understanding?"
msgstr "Piksa i sapotim tok bilong tekst o nogat? Taim ol i ritim dispela hap, piksa i helpim ol long save?"

#: temp.glade:29572
msgid "In the context of this passage, is it clear \n"
"what is happening in this image?"
msgstr "Long dispela hap tok, ating klia long wanem samting i kamap long dispela piksa?"

#: temp.glade:29584
msgid "For example, do the colors have the same meaning in the local culture? Is there anything in the background that is distracting from the story? Are there any objects, gestures, or other things that imply something unintended or that isn’t in the passage? Are there any anachronisms in the picture (a minaret in Bethlehem)?"
msgstr "Olsem, ol kala i gat wankain minin long ples bilong yupela? I gat wanpela samting long baksait i save paulim tingting long stori? I gat wanpela samting, pasin bilong han o narapela samting i makim wanpela tok i no stap long dispela hap tok? I gat wanpela samting long piksa i no stret long taim (olsem wanpela minaret long Betlehem)?"

#: temp.glade:29586
msgid "Does the image communicate something \n"
"that it should not in this particular context?"
msgstr "Dispela piksa i soim wanpela samting\n"
"em i no ken soim long dispela taim?"

#: temp.glade:29598
msgid "Do the images and their style fit with the type of publication, i.e. Scripture, children’s materials, lectionary, etc.? Are people and actions depicted in acceptable ways?"
msgstr "Ol piksa na stail bilong ol i stret long kain buk yupela i wokim, olsem Skripsa, ol buk bilong ol pikinini, lektionari, na ol narapela? Ol man na ol pasin i soim long piksa, i orait long ol man?"

#: temp.glade:29600
msgid "Is the image appropriate for the publication?"
msgstr "Dispela piksa i stret long dispela buk?"

#: temp.glade:29613
msgid "Select the level to which this illustration\n"
"is acceptable in the receptor culture."
msgstr "Makim hamas dispela piksa\n"
"i orait long kalsa bilong ol man i kisim."

#: temp.glade:29630
msgid "OK to\n"
"mirror"
msgstr "I OK long\n"
"mirror"

#: temp.glade:29636
msgid "It is fine to mirror the image if needed. It would\n"
"not change the impact or response of the readers."
msgstr "I orait long mirrorim dispela piksa sapos i gat bikpela as. Dispela i no senisim tingting o bekim bilong ol man i ritim."

#: temp.glade:29651
msgid "Never\n"
"mirror"
msgstr "Nogat\n"
"mirror"

#: temp.glade:29657
msgid "Ensure that this image is always shown\n"
"as currently depicted in the preview. Do\n"
"NOT allow it to be mirrored (reversed)."
msgstr "Mekim sure dispela piksa i stap oltaim\n"
"olsem em i stap long preview nau. Nogat\n"
"mirrorim (tainim) em."

#: temp.glade:29673
msgid "Always\n"
"mirror"
msgstr "Oltaim\n"
"mirror"

#: temp.glade:29679
msgid "Ensure that this image is always mirrored from\n"
"what is currently shown in the preview. Therefore\n"
"actions being done with the left hand will show as\n"
"being done with the right hand, and vice versa."
msgstr "Mekim sure dispela piksa i stap mirror oltaim\n"
"bilong dispela i stap long preview nau. Olsem na\n"
"wok ol i mekim long han kais bai i kamap olsem\n"
"ol i mekim long han skru, na sem tasol."

#: temp.glade:29700
msgid "Select the reason for including the\n"
"illustration in this particular publication."
msgstr "Makim as bilong putim dispela\n"
"piksa long dispela buk."

#: temp.glade:29753 temp.glade:29839
msgid "Unchecked"
msgstr "I no gat setik"

#: temp.glade:29811
msgid "Select the appropriateness of the\n"
"illustration within this publication."
msgstr "Makim olsem wanem dispela piksa\n"
"i stret long dispela buk."

#: temp.glade:29862
msgid "Consultant Approval:"
msgstr "Konsultan i orait:"

#: temp.glade:29879
msgid "The most recent date that the\n"
"consultant approval updated."
msgstr "Las dei long konsultan i senisim\n"
"orait bilong em."

#: temp.glade:29885
msgid "Date"
msgstr "Dei"

#: temp.glade:29902
msgid "Initials"
msgstr "Nem bilong yu (initial)"

#: temp.glade:29916
msgid "any publication"
msgstr "olgeta buk"

#: temp.glade:29933
msgid "this publication"
msgstr "dispela buk"

#: temp.glade:29950
msgid "Approved to\n"
"be used in:"
msgstr "I orait long\n"
"yusim long:"

#: temp.glade:29969
msgid "     "
msgstr ""

#: temp.glade:29982
msgid "By:"
msgstr "Long:"

#: temp.glade:30051
msgid "Notes About This Picture:"
msgstr "Ol not long dispela piksa:"

#: temp.glade:30131
msgid "Pictures are best used in situations where:\n"
"1. The physical situation is not understood, or not common in the target culture.\n"
"2. Where the physical situation is important to understanding the meaning of the passage (e.g., the type of clothing is often not important, but in some passages it might be).\n"
"3. Where they help the reader to understand the passage.\n"
"4. Where it entices the reader to read the passage."
msgstr "Ol piksa i gutpela long ol taim olsem:\n"
"1. Ol man i no save long dispela samting, o i no planti long kalsa bilong ol.\n"
"2. Samting long ai i bikpela long save long minin bilong dispela hap tok (olsem, kain laplap i no save bikpela, tasol long sampela hap tok em i ken bikpela).\n"
"3. Ol i helpim man i ritim long kliaim dispela hap tok.\n"
"4. Ol i pulim tingting bilong man long ritim dispela hap tok."

#: temp.glade:30136
msgid "Questions to Consider"
msgstr "Ol Askim long Skelim"

#: temp.glade:30165
msgid "This tab encourages you to think through\n"
"the appropriateness of the pictures used\n"
"in this publication, as well as other contexts."
msgstr "Dispela tab i helpim yu long tingting gut\n"
"long ol piksa yu yusim long dispela buk,\n"
"na long ol narapela ples tu."

#: temp.glade:30168
msgid "Checklist"
msgstr "Lis bilong Skelim"

#: temp.glade:30263
msgid "Manipulate the pictures to be used\n"
"in the publication. Control everything\n"
"from quality to position, from captions\n"
"to copyrights."
msgstr "Stretim ol piksa bilong ol i go insait\n"
"long buk. Yu ken kontrolim olgeta samting\n"
"stat long kwaliti na ples, na tu ol caption\n"
"na ol kopirait."

#: temp.glade:30312
msgid "Use Default Header Settings for Diglot"
msgstr "Yusim Seting Bilong Header i Stap Pastaim Long Diglot"

#: temp.glade:30317
msgid "Checking this option will override\n"
"the header settings and place the\n"
"Reference Ranges on the outer edges\n"
"and Page Number in (or near) the middle."
msgstr "Sapos yu makim dispela, ol seting bilong header\n"
"i no moa wok, na ol Reference Ranges bai i go\n"
"long ol sait ausait na namba bilong pes bai i stap\n"
"long namel (o klostu long namel)."

#: temp.glade:30333
msgid "Adjust Center Header Based on Column Widths"
msgstr "Senisim Header Namel Folim Bikpela Bilong Ol Kolum"

#: temp.glade:30338
msgid "If the column widths of the two sides of the\n"
"diglot are unequal, PTXprint can ensure that\n"
"the content of the center header matches the\n"
"position of the gutter (space between the two\n"
"different columns)."
msgstr "Sapos ol kolum long tupela sait bilong diglot\n"
"i no wankain bikpela, PTXprint i ken mekim\n"
"olsem ol samting long header namel i stap\n"
"stret long gutter (spes namel long tupela\n"
"kolum)."

#: temp.glade:30376
msgid "Vertical Rule in Notes Area"
msgstr "Vertikal Rule Long Ples Bilong Ol Nout"

#: temp.glade:30381
msgid "Add a vertical rule between the two\n"
"sides of the notes area of the diglot."
msgstr "Putim wanpela vertikal rule namel long tupela\n"
"sait bilong ples bilong ol nout bilong diglot."

#: temp.glade:30396
msgid "Join with Rule Above"
msgstr "Joinim Wantaim Rule i Stap Antap"

#: temp.glade:30401
msgid "To prevent a small gap in the line\n"
"allow the vertical line to extend\n"
"down into the notes area."
msgstr "Bilong stopim liklik spes long lain,\n"
"larim vertikal lain i go daun\n"
"long ples bilong ol nout."

#: temp.glade:30420
msgid "Separate Notes in Two Columns"
msgstr "Katim Ol Nout Long Tupela Kolum"

#: temp.glade:30425
msgid "If this option is disabled, the footnotes from\n"
"both sides of the diglot get merged together\n"
"and are interspersed one after the other.\n"
"\n"
"Depending on the scripts and text direction,\n"
"this may or may not be desirable. If in doubt,\n"
"leave this option checked ON."
msgstr "Sapos dispela i no makim, ol futnout\n"
"bilong tupela sait bilong diglot i kamap wantaim\n"
"na i stap wan bihain long narapela.\n"
"\n"
"Tingting long ol skripsa na direksen bilong tok,\n"
"sampela taim dispela i gutpela o i no gutpela.\n"
"Sapos yu no save, larim dispela i stap makim (ON)."

